# minimal-intervention-component-preservation

Scope every intervention to the minimum set of affected components. Pristine or unaffected parts must not be modified. Installation and removal techniques must avoid collateral damage (e.g., side loads, full teardowns when a partial disassembly suffices).

## Procedures
- Before disassembly, identify only the components that must be removed to reach the defect; leave all others in place.
- During installation, select techniques that transfer force axially (e.g., drift for bearing press-fit) rather than laterally.
- Never modify, rework, or handle pristine components (e.g., rotor) unless the task explicitly requires it.
- After rework, reinstall only the components that were removed.

## Conventions
- Full teardown is reserved for cases where partial disassembly is geometrically impossible.
- Installation tools must not apply side load to interference-fit components.

